Soundpost version-pinned generic regular-expression and Unicode primitives

This directory contains generic library code, not a telemetry query engine.

The original regexp, regexp/syntax and unicode source files retain their
original The Go Authors copyright headers and BSD-3-Clause license. They are
NOT relicensed as Soundpost first-party Apache-2.0 code. Full original license
texts are retained in go123/LICENSE, go124/LICENSE and go126/LICENSE.

Original source:
- github.com/grafana/regexp v0.0.0-20240518133315-a468a5bfb3bc
- github.com/grafana/regexp v0.0.0-20250905093917-f7b3be9d1853
- golang/go tags go1.23.4, go1.24.5 and go1.26.10, src/regexp/syntax and src/unicode

Exact source URLs, module zip hashes, original file SHA256 hashes, vendored file
SHA256 hashes, modifications, and license hash are recorded in sources.json.
Module ZIP bytes came directly from proxy.golang.org; stdlib source bytes came
directly from raw.githubusercontent.com/golang/go at the specified tags.
No code was extracted from Loki's AGPL implementation or translated from its
parser, evaluator, templates, optimization tables or corpus.

Modifications to original source are limited to import relocation and one
pooled checkedInput field on each regexp machine. Unmodified Unicode data is
version-specific: all three editions report Unicode15.0.0, but Go1.26.10 adds
category/name-dispatch data that must not be substituted into older editions.

The separate regexp/context.go files are independently authored Soundpost
execution/cancellation adapters, Copyright 2026 Aryn Yklas, Apache-2.0 (the
repository LICENSE). They do not replace, relicense or claim authorship of the
original matching algorithms. They run the original NFA with cancellable
string input, preserving absolute anchor context and capture semantics.
